    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16480" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēvĭdentĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f.
		evidens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>clearness</i>, <i>distinctness.</i>—In rhet. lang., <i>clearness</i>, <i>perspicuity;</i> used by
			Cicero along with perspicuitas, as a transl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνάργεια</span>. <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Ac. 2, 6, 17</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 6,
				2, 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 2,
			63</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 2,
			40</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A proof</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magna suae ostensionis,</span>”
				<i>of his own manifestation</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2
					Macc. 3, 24</span></i>
			.</div>
